% DMEPOS: the rules that every DME MAC policy shares, as a library for the
% policy programs of this directory (pap.le, oxygen.le, pmd.le, ...). The
% RulesRUs report, §2.1, is the plan; README.md the method and the results.
%
% Texts: the Standard Documentation Requirements article A55426 (the standard
% written order, the written order prior to delivery, the face-to-face
% encounter, proof of delivery, continued need and use, refills); 42 CFR
% 410.38 (the conditions of payment those requirements come from, and the
% place where DME may be used); the Medicare Benefit Policy Manual, Chapter
% 15, §110.1 (what durable medical equipment is); the CMS Required Face-to-Face
% Encounter and Written Order Prior to Delivery List and the Required Prior
% Authorization List (which codes each applies to).
%
% Findings. Many criteria are clinical findings about the beneficiary ("the
% mobility limitation cannot be resolved by a cane or walker", "oxygen will
% improve the condition"): the treating practitioner's note states them, a
% reviewer or an appeal body accepts or rejects them. They are one judged
% template, "the finding F about B is established / unsupported", recorded
% with who found it and why; a finding nobody has made leaves the answer
% conditional (a judgment needed), as in the customs model.
%
% How a claim is read. A claim is for one item (a device, an accessory, a
% supply), coded with its HCPCS code, furnished to a beneficiary, on a date of
% service, for a rental month (1, 2, 3, ... — absent for a purchase or a
% one-off supply) or as a refill of a supply. The policy programs say when a
% claim is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY (the coverage criteria of the LCD, Social
% Security Act §1862(a)(1)(A)) — the question the appeal record decides. This
% library says when a claim is PAYABLE: it is within the scope of a modelled
% policy (applicability), the item is within a Medicare benefit category and
% used in a home, it is reasonable and necessary (question), and the order,
% face-to-face, delivery, prior-authorization, continued-need and refill
% requirements are met (remedy). Nothing not stated is met: the facts of a
% claim are what its documentation shows, each with its source.
%
% Every rule cites the passage it encodes; the documents say where they are
% published and where their text is (sources/). Rules that are this model's
% own devices have no provenance and say so in a comment. Six months is read
% as 183 days and twelve months as 365 days, LE having day arithmetic only.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the claim and the item
    *a claim* is for *an item*; undefined.
    the HCPCS code of *an item* is *a code*; undefined.
    *an item* is furnished to *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the date of service of *a claim* is *a date*; undefined.
    the rental month of *a claim* is *a number*; undefined.
    *a claim* is a refill; undefined.
    *a claim* was submitted on *a date*; undefined.
    the quantity billed on *a claim* is *a number*; undefined.
    *a claim* is for a supply of *a number* months; undefined.
    *an item* is an accessory of *a device*; undefined.
    % the record of the order, the encounter and the delivery
    the order for *an item* is dated *a date*; undefined.
    the order for *an item* is signed by the treating practitioner; undefined.
    the order for *an item* includes *an element*; undefined.
    the order for *an item* was communicated to the supplier on *a date*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner examined *a beneficiary* for *an item* in a face-to-face encounter on *a date*; undefined.
    *an item* was delivered on *a date*; undefined.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for *an item*; undefined.
    prior authorization for *an item* was affirmed on *a date*; undefined.
    the medical record documents continued need for *an item* on *a date*; undefined.
    the record documents continued use of *an item* on *a date*; undefined.
    the current supply of *an item* is expected to end on *a date*; undefined.
    the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of *an item* on *a date*; undefined.
    the medical record of *a beneficiary* documents *a condition*; undefined.
    % a finding of the record, the reviewer or the appeal body about the beneficiary
    the finding *a finding* about *a beneficiary* is *an outcome*; judged.
    % what the record states about the beneficiary and the selection of the
    % item, read by several policies
    the weight of *a beneficiary* is *a number* pounds; undefined.
    the diagnosis code of *a beneficiary* is *a code*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* had a specialty evaluation by a licensed medical professional with no financial relationship with the supplier for *an item*; undefined.
    a RESNA certified assistive technology professional employed by the supplier was directly involved in the selection of *an item*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has been self propelling a manual wheelchair for at least one year; undefined.
    % where the beneficiary lives, and what the item is
    the residence of *a beneficiary* is *a place*; undefined.
    *an item* can withstand repeated use; undefined.
    *an item* is primarily and customarily used to serve a medical purpose; undefined.
    *an item* is generally not useful to a person in the absence of illness or injury; undefined.
    *an item* is appropriate for use in the home; undefined.
    % derived
    *a claim* is within the scope of the model.
    the policy of *a claim* is *a policy*.
    the policy for code *a code* is *a policy*.
    the benefit category of code *a code* is *a category*.
    *an item* is within a Medicare benefit category.
    *an item* is durable medical equipment.
    *a place* qualifies as a home.
    *a place* is excluded from being a home.
    *a claim* is reasonable and necessary.
    *a claim* is payable.
    the order requirements are met for *an item*.
    the order for *an item* is a complete standard written order.
    *an element* is a required element of a standard written order.
    the timing requirements of the order for *an item* are met.
    the face-to-face requirement is met for *an item*.
    *a code* is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list.
    *a code* is on the required prior authorization list.
    the delivery requirements are met for *a claim*.
    the prior authorization requirement is met for *an item*.
    the continued need requirements are met for *a claim*.
    *a claim* is an ongoing claim.
    the refill requirements are met for *a claim*.
    the policy specific documentation requirements are met for *a claim*.
    *a policy* has no specific documentation requirements.

the knowledge base dmepos includes:

% The cited documents: where they are published, and a copy of their text.
Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=55426".
the text of Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426 is at "sources/article/A55426.txt".
42 CFR section 410 38 is published at "https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-42/chapter-IV/subchapter-B/part-410/subpart-B/section-410.38".
the text of 42 CFR section 410 38 is at "sources/cfr/42_CFR_410.38.txt".
Medicare Benefit Policy Manual Chapter 15 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/regulations-and-guidance/guidance/manuals/downloads/bp102c15.pdf".
the text of Medicare Benefit Policy Manual Chapter 15 is at "sources/manuals/BPM_100-02_ch15.txt".
the CMS required face-to-face list is published at "https://www.cms.gov/files/document/required-face-face-encounter-written-order-prior-delivery-list.pdf".
the text of the CMS required face-to-face list is at "sources/cfr/CMS_required_f2f_wopd_list_2026-04-13.txt".
the CMS required prior authorization list is published at "https://www.cms.gov/research-statistics-data-and-systems/monitoring-programs/medicare-ffs-compliance-programs/dmepos/downloads/dmepos_pa_required-prior-authorization-list.pdf".
the text of the CMS required prior authorization list is at "sources/cfr/CMS_required_prior_authorization_list_2026-07-29.txt".

% What durable medical equipment is (the Manual's definition), for an item
% whose code no policy places in a benefit.
rule dme_definition with provenance Medicare Benefit Policy Manual Chapter 15,
        confer "Can withstand repeated use":
an item is durable medical equipment
    if the item can withstand repeated use
    and the item is primarily and customarily used to serve a medical purpose
    and the item is generally not useful to a person in the absence of illness or injury
    and the item is appropriate for use in the home.

% The policy of a claim: outside the section checklist, so a guard such as
% "the policy of the claim is pmd" in another policy's rule does not charge
% a claim's failure to applicability.
rule claim_policy:
the policy of a claim is a policy
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the policy for code the code is the policy.

section applicability is:

% A claim the model can decide: its item's code belongs to a policy this
% directory models (each policy program lists its codes). A device of this
% model.
rule scope:
a claim is within the scope of the model
    if the policy of the claim is a policy.

% The benefit category: the item is of a kind the policy places in a benefit
% (the policy programs say so, code by code), or it is durable medical
% equipment by the Manual's definition; and it is used in the home.
rule benefit_category_by_code with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Medicare Part B pays for durable medical equipment, including ventilators, oxygen equipment, hospital beds, and wheelchairs, if the equipment is used in the patient's home or in an institution that is used as a home":
an item is within a Medicare benefit category
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the benefit category of code the code is durable medical equipment
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the residence of the beneficiary is a place
    and the place qualifies as a home.

% a benefit other than durable medical equipment (therapeutic shoes,
% prosthetics, orthotics) carries no condition on the place of use
rule benefit_category_other with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Medicare Part B pays for durable medical equipment, including ventilators, oxygen equipment, hospital beds, and wheelchairs, if the equipment is used in the patient's home or in an institution that is used as a home":
an item is within a Medicare benefit category
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the benefit category of code the code is a category
    and it is not the case that
        the benefit category of code the code is durable medical equipment.

rule benefit_category_by_definition with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Medicare Part B pays for durable medical equipment, including ventilators, oxygen equipment, hospital beds, and wheelchairs, if the equipment is used in the patient's home or in an institution that is used as a home":
an item is within a Medicare benefit category
    if the item is durable medical equipment
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the residence of the beneficiary is a place
    and the place qualifies as a home.

rule home with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "An institution that is used as a home may not be a hospital or a CAH or a SNF":
a place qualifies as a home
    if it is not the case that
        the place is excluded from being a home.

hospital is excluded from being a home,
    as stated in 42 CFR section 410 38, confer "An institution that is used as a home may not be a hospital or a CAH or a SNF".
critical access hospital is excluded from being a home,
    as stated in 42 CFR section 410 38, confer "An institution that is used as a home may not be a hospital or a CAH or a SNF".
skilled nursing facility is excluded from being a home,
    as stated in 42 CFR section 410 38, confer "An institution that is used as a home may not be a hospital or a CAH or a SNF".

section remedy is:

% Payment: the coverage question answered, and the conditions of payment met.
rule payable with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "In the event of a claim review, a DMEPOS supplier must provide sufficient information to demonstrate that the applicable criteria have been met thus justifying payment":
a claim is payable
    if the claim is within the scope of the model
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is within a Medicare benefit category
    and the claim is reasonable and necessary
    and the order requirements are met for the item
    and the delivery requirements are met for the claim
    and the prior authorization requirement is met for the item
    and the continued need requirements are met for the claim
    and the refill requirements are met for the claim
    and the policy specific documentation requirements are met for the claim.

% Each policy either states that it has no documentation requirements of its
% own or defines them (a power mobility device: the order written by the
% practitioner who examined the beneficiary, the home assessment, delivery
% within six months of the prior authorization). A device of this model.
rule no_policy_specific_documentation:
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is a policy
    and the policy has no specific documentation requirements.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The order: a standard written order, its timing, the face-to-face encounter.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule order_requirements with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "All claims for items billed to Medicare require a written order/prescription from the treating practitioner as a condition for payment":
the order requirements are met for an item
    if the order for the item is a complete standard written order
    and the timing requirements of the order for the item are met
    and the face-to-face requirement is met for the item.

rule swo_elements with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "A SWO must contain all of the following elements":
the order for an item is a complete standard written order
    if the order for the item is dated a date
    and the order for the item is signed by the treating practitioner
    and for all cases in which
            an element is a required element of a standard written order
        it is the case that
            the order for the item includes the element.

beneficiary name is a required element of a standard written order,
    as stated in Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426, confer "Beneficiary's name or Medicare Beneficiary Identifier (MBI)".
order date is a required element of a standard written order,
    as stated in Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426, confer "Order Date".
description of the item is a required element of a standard written order,
    as stated in Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426, confer "General description of the item".
quantity to be dispensed is a required element of a standard written order,
    as stated in Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426, confer "Quantity to be dispensed, if applicable".
treating practitioner name is a required element of a standard written order,
    as stated in Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426, confer "Treating Practitioner Name or NPI".

% Timing: an item on the Required List needs the order before delivery; any
% other item before the claim is submitted — which is certainly so when the
% order reached the supplier by the date of service.
rule wopd with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "For PMDs and other DMEPOS items selected for inclusion on the Required Face-to-Face Encounter and Written Order Prior to Delivery List, the written order/prescription must be communicated to the supplier prior to delivery":
the timing requirements of the order for an item are met
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list
    and the order for the item was communicated to the supplier on a date
    and the item was delivered on an other date
    and the date is before or equal to the other date.

rule swo_before_submission with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "For all other DMEPOS, the written order/prescription must be communicated to the supplier prior to claim submission":
the timing requirements of the order for an item are met
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list
    and the order for the item was communicated to the supplier on a date
    and a claim is for the item
    and the claim was submitted on an other date
    and the date is before or equal to the other date.

rule swo_before_service with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "For all other DMEPOS, the written order/prescription must be communicated to the supplier prior to claim submission":
the timing requirements of the order for an item are met
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list
    and the order for the item was communicated to the supplier on a date
    and a claim is for the item
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the date is before or equal to the other date.

rule face_to_face with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "the treating practitioner must document and communicate to the DMEPOS supplier that the treating practitioner has had a face-to-face encounter with the beneficiary within the 6 months preceding the date of the written order/prescription":
the face-to-face requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the order for the item is dated a date
    and the treating practitioner examined the beneficiary for the item in a face-to-face encounter on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 183.

rule face_to_face_not_required with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Items Requiring a Face-to-Face Encounter":
the face-to-face requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list.

% The Required Face-to-Face Encounter and Written Order Prior to Delivery
% List (42 CFR 410.38(c)(8)), edition effective 13 April 2026 with the oxygen
% codes, as published for 28 October 2026: manual wheelchairs, oxygen, power
% mobility devices, ventilators, osteogenesis stimulators, TENS, hospital
% beds, support surfaces, orthoses.
a code is on the required face-to-face and written order prior to delivery list
    if the code is in ["K0002", "K0003", "K0004", "K0005", "K0006", "K0007", "K0738", "E0194", "E0290", "E0301", "E0304", "E0424", "E0431", "E0433", "E0434", "E0439", "E1390", "E1391", "E1392", "E0466", "E0467", "E0468", "E0747", "E0748", "E0760", "E1161", "K0800", "K0801", "K0802", "K0806", "K0807", "K0808", "K0813", "K0814", "K0815", "K0816", "K0820", "K0821", "K0822", "K0823", "K0824", "K0825", "K0826", "K0827", "K0828", "K0829", "K0831", "K0835", "K0836", "K0837", "K0838", "K0839", "K0840", "K0841", "K0842", "K0843", "K0848", "K0849", "K0850", "K0851", "K0852", "K0853", "K0854", "K0855", "K0856", "K0857", "K0858", "K0859", "K0860", "K0861", "K0862", "K0863", "K0864", "L0456", "L0457", "L0486", "L0631", "L0635", "L0636", "L0637", "L0638", "L0639", "L0640", "L0648", "L0650", "L0651", "L1832", "L1833", "L1843", "L1845", "L1851", "L1852", "L1906", "L1932", "L1933", "L1940", "L1951", "L1952", "L1960", "L1970", "L2005", "L2036", "L3761", "L3916", "L3960"].

% The Required Prior Authorization List (42 CFR 414.234(c)(1)), updated 29
% July 2026: power mobility devices, support surfaces, lower limb prostheses,
% orthoses, pneumatic compression devices, the ultralightweight wheelchair.
a code is on the required prior authorization list
    if the code is in ["E0193", "E0194", "E0277", "E0371", "E0372", "E0373", "E0651", "E0652", "K0005", "K0800", "K0801", "K0802", "K0806", "K0807", "K0808", "K0813", "K0814", "K0815", "K0816", "K0820", "K0821", "K0822", "K0823", "K0824", "K0825", "K0826", "K0827", "K0828", "K0829", "K0835", "K0836", "K0837", "K0838", "K0839", "K0840", "K0841", "K0842", "K0843", "K0848", "K0849", "K0850", "K0851", "K0852", "K0853", "K0854", "K0855", "K0856", "K0857", "K0858", "K0859", "K0860", "K0861", "K0862", "K0863", "K0864", "L0456", "L0457", "L0486", "L0631", "L0637", "L0639", "L0648", "L0650", "L0651", "L1832", "L1833", "L1843", "L1844", "L1845", "L1846", "L1851", "L1852", "L1932", "L1951", "L3761", "L3916", "L5856", "L5857", "L5858", "L5973", "L5980", "L5987"].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Delivery, prior authorization, continued need and use, refills.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule proof_of_delivery with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "All services that do not have appropriate POD from the supplier will be denied and overpayments will be requested":
the delivery requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item was delivered on a date
    and the supplier holds proof of delivery for the item.

rule prior_authorization with provenance the CMS required prior authorization list,
        confer "REQUIRED PRIOR AUTHORIZATION LIST As defined in 42 CFR 414.234(c)(1)":
the prior authorization requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is on the required prior authorization list
    and prior authorization for the item was affirmed on a date.

rule prior_authorization_not_required with provenance the CMS required prior authorization list,
        confer "REQUIRED PRIOR AUTHORIZATION LIST As defined in 42 CFR 414.234(c)(1)":
the prior authorization requirement is met for an item
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and it is not the case that
        the code is on the required prior authorization list.

% An ongoing claim — a rental month after the first, or a refill of supplies —
% needs timely documentation of continued need and of continued use: a record
% in the preceding twelve months.
rule ongoing_rental:
a claim is an ongoing claim
    if the rental month of the claim is a number
    and the number > 1.

rule ongoing_refill:
a claim is an ongoing claim
    if the claim is a refill.

rule continued_need with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "For ongoing supplies and rented DME items, in addition to information described above that justifies the initial provision of the item(s) and/or supplies, there must be information in the beneficiary’s medical record to support that the item continues to remain reasonable and necessary":
the continued need requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is an ongoing claim
    and the claim is for an item
    and the date of service of the claim is a date
    and the medical record documents continued need for the item on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 365
    and the record documents continued use of the item on a third date
    and the date is a second number days after the third date
    and the second number >= 0
    and the second number <= 365.

rule initial_claim_need with provenance Standard Documentation Requirements Article A55426,
        confer "For all DMEPOS items, the initial justification for medical need is established at the time the item(s) is first ordered":
the continued need requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is an ongoing claim.

rule refill with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Contact and affirmative response must be within 30 calendar days from the expected end of the current supply":
the refill requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is a refill
    and the claim is for an item
    and the current supply of the item is expected to end on a date
    and the beneficiary affirmed the need for the refill of the item on an other date
    and the date is a number days after the other date
    and the number >= 0
    and the number <= 30
    and the date of service of the claim is a third date
    and the date is a second number days after the third date
    and the second number <= 10.

rule not_a_refill with provenance 42 CFR section 410 38,
        confer "Refills mean DMEPOS products that are provided on a recurring basis secondary to a medically necessary DMEPOS order":
the refill requirements are met for a claim
    if the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the claim is a refill.
